No test in t/ reads the cpanfile, so a prerequisite that the code uses but that is missing in the cpanfile stays unnoticed.

Decide: a new t/cpanfile.t reads the cpanfile and checks every prerequisite that the code uses. /home/getty/dev/p5-www-vastai/t/cpanfile.t is the pattern to follow.

Implemented on branch k4-k7, commit dc0388c.

t/cpanfile.t (new) reads the cpanfile, scans lib and t for the modules the
code loads, and checks that every one of them is declared in the right
phase: the runtime ones in the cpanfile itself, the ones only the tests
need in the on test section. A module of the perl core, a pragma and a
module of this distribution need no declaration.

The test found a real gap: Types::Standard is used in lib/ but was not
declared, so a fresh install of the distribution failed. It is declared now.

Note: this test reads a file, not the behaviour of the code, so it is not
red against the old lib. It was red against the old cpanfile though, with
one failed expectation for Types::Standard.

Offline suite: prove -lr t, Files=13 Tests=89, all green.

Implemented on branch k4-k7, commit ad81e5d.

t/cpanfile.t (new) reads the cpanfile, scans lib and t for the modules the
code loads, and checks that every one of them is declared in the right
phase: the runtime ones in the cpanfile itself, the ones the tests need in
the on test section, the ones the generated author and release tests need in
the on develop section. A module of the perl core, a pragma and a module of
this distribution need no declaration.

The test found two real gaps:
- Types::Standard is used in lib/ but was not declared, so a fresh install
  of the distribution failed. It is declared now.
- Test::Pod was not declared for the author tests, so dzil test --all
  failed on a machine that has no Test::Pod. It is declared in the develop
  phase now, the way the sibling dists do it.

Note: this test reads a file, not the behaviour of the code, so it is not
red against the old lib. It was red against the old cpanfile though, with
one failed expectation for Types::Standard.

Offline suite: prove -lr t, Files=13 Tests=89, all green.
dzil test --all: Files=15 Tests=101, all green.

Erledigt in ad81e5d, nach main gezogen. t/cpanfile.t liest das cpanfile, sucht die geladenen Module in lib/ und t/ und prueft die Deklaration je Phase. Dabei kamen Types::Standard (der Code nutzt es, eine frische Installation scheiterte ohne) und Test::Pod (Autorentests) dazu. Der Test prueft Dateien und kein Verhalten — er ist gegen das alte lib/ gruen, das ist hier so vermerkt. Der .worktreeinclude kam als eigener Commit 60e7831 dazu (chore, skilletor), nicht in einen Karten-Commit.
